  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>rms</mi></math> speed of oxygen molecule in a vessel at particular temperature is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;when&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>&nbsp;is the average speed of the molecule. The value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;will be:</p><p>(take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>22</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math>)</p>",
    "image": null
  },
